org.liberty.gchb.messages=Fixed the bug. Now it just crashes differently. | Added a feature. Hope no one notices the bugs I introduced. |  Refactored code. Even I don't know how it works now. | Committing all changes before I break everything. | Who needs documentation when you have magic? | I have no idea what I'm doing, but it works! | Bug? What bug? I call it an undocumented feature. | Merge conflict resolved. Probably. | Made the code more confusing. You're welcome. | Temporarily fixed. Awaiting future disaster. | YOLO commit - no testing, no regrets. | Removed console.log. Code should now work in production. | Works on my machine. Good luck! | Deleted all TODO comments. Problem solved. | Hacky fix for an unexplainable bug. Hope no one notices. | Code so bad, even AI refuses to explain it. | Changed something. Let's see what breaks. | It compiles. Ship it! | Half-baked feature, full-baked confidence. | Stack Overflow-driven development at its finest. | Reverted previous commit. I regret nothing. | Improved performance by deleting half the code. | Committing this before I change my mind. | Oops. This was meant for a different branch. | This commit is a cry for help.